---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy | Isaac Assistant" description="Privacy policy for Isaac Assistant, a private personal tool.">
	<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
	<p class="muted">Last updated: 27 September 2026</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Isaac Assistant</strong> is a private, personal tool built and used only by Isaac Egglestone to organise his
		own Gmail and Google Calendar alongside his work schedule. It is not offered to the public.
	</p>

	<h2>What data it accesses</h2>
	<p>With the account owner's explicit consent through Google's sign-in screen, the tool may access:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Gmail messages and labels (to read, label and archive email)</li>
		<li>Google Calendar events (to read and create events)</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How data is used</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Data is processed only on the owner's own computer, to help him manage his email and calendar.</li>
		<li>Data is not sold, shared with third parties, or used for advertising.</li>
		<li>Data is not stored on any server run by this tool. OAuth tokens are held in the owner's local operating-system keychain.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Use of information received from Google APIs follows the
		<a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
		including the Limited Use requirements.
	</p>

	<h2>Revoking access</h2>
	<p>
		You can remove the tool's access at any time from
		<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account → Third-party connections</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>Questions can be raised through <a href="https://github.com/isaacegglestone">GitHub</a>.</p>
</Base>
